Allow root agents to resume durable goals

Paused and blocked goals currently require an app-server caller to
reactivate them. An explicit user request therefore cannot be honored
by a running root agent without granting the model the broader
update_goal transition.

Add a root-only Saffron tool backed by a goal-extension capability
that owns conditional persistence and runtime effects. Resumption now
preserves goal identity and accounting while rejecting stale, active,
exhausted, or completed goals.
